episode_metadata.question:
The planet Xavier follows an elliptical orbit with its sun at one focus.  At its nearest point (perigee), it is 2 astronomical units (AU) from the sun, while at its furthest point (apogee) it is X AU away.  When Xavier is midway along its orbit, as shown, how far is it from the sun, in AU?

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

path ell = xscale(2)*arc((0,0),1,-85,265);

filldraw(Circle((0,-1),0.1));
filldraw(Circle((-1.4,0),0.2),yellow);
draw(ell,Arrow(6));
[/asy]
If we know the answer to the above question is 7, what is the value of unknown variable X?

